# Persist chats and plans

Cursor chats, transcripts, and plans under `~/.cursor` are **not** in git.
A `git clone` of the last pushed commit on another PC must be enough to
continue this work. Anything we want kept must be a file in this repo.

## On “save the chat” (also when the user asks to commit and push notes)

Do all of these, in order:

1. Write or append `notes/chats/YYYY-MM-DD-short-slug.md` (decisions and
   rationale, not tool traces).
2. Scan `~/.cursor/plans/` and the workspace `.cursor/plans/` for
   **this project’s** `.plan.md` files, including drafts and superseded
   versions. Copy new or changed files into `notes/plans/cursor/` using
   the original `slug_hash.plan.md` filename so later saves overwrite
   the same id.
3. Update standing plans under `notes/plans/` if the session changed them.
4. Commit and **push**. Clone-of-HEAD is the bar.

## Which plans belong here

Only flt-compression. Match by content (`flt-compression`,
`vendor/fermats-last-theorem`, `unification-opportunities`, `FinalCheck`)
or by being created in this workspace. Do **not** copy the rest of
`~/.cursor/plans/` (other repos on this machine).

## Layout

- `notes/chats/` — session write-ups
- `notes/plans/` — standing plans you step through
- `notes/plans/cursor/` — verbatim Cursor plans
- `sources/` — working lists and images

Do not rely on agent-transcripts or the chat UI as the archive.
A clone will not have Lean/`lake` caches or Cursor UI transcripts;
those can be rebuilt. Planning state cannot.
